---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Economy · Meridian"
  description="A live read on the Meridian server economy: the Meridian Economic Index, money supply, trade volume, prices, and player wealth."
  path="/economy"
  analytics
>
<main class="doc">
  <h1>Economy</h1>
  <p class="lead">A live read on the Meridian economy, rebuilt from server data. See the <a href="/faq#economy">FAQ</a> for how the economy works.</p>
  <div class="data-stale" data-stale hidden></div>

  <div class="analytics" data-analytics>
    <!-- Ordered the way an economic report is ordered: the rules of the
         economy first, then money, prices, activity and distribution. Each
         figure appears exactly once, with the chart it belongs to. -->
    <section id="flow">
      <h2>How money works</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">Where currency enters the economy and where it is destroyed. Everything else only moves money between players.</p>
      <div class="flow-grid">
        <div class="flow-col flow-source">
          <h3>Sources</h3>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Starting balance</span><span class="f-val">$2,500</span><span class="f-note">once, per new player</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Voting</span><span class="f-val">no cash</span><span class="f-note">pays a crate and a vote point, deliberately never money</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Sell counter</span><span class="f-val">floor price</span><span class="f-note">raw metals and minerals, marked down permanently as it buys</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-col flow-sink">
          <h3>Sinks</h3>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Land claims</span><span class="f-val">$250/chunk</span><span class="f-note">flat, first chunk free</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Land upkeep</span><span class="f-val">$100/chunk</span><span class="f-note">weekly, per claimed chunk</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Nation founding</span><span class="f-val">$35,000</span><span class="f-note">once</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Nation upkeep</span><span class="f-val">$40/chunk</span><span class="f-note">weekly, across all member lands</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Buy counter</span><span class="f-val">premium price</span><span class="f-note">50 items, priced above the player market on purpose</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Crates</span><span class="f-val">$1,000 / $2,800 / $6,500</span><span class="f-note">Iron, Gold and Diamond. Cash back is a rare jackpot</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Ranks</span><span class="f-val">$12,000 to $120,000</span><span class="f-note">Citizen, Landholder, Magnate, Sovereign</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 id="dynamic">Dynamic pricing</h3>
      <p class="as-sub">Every unit the Sell counter buys lowers that item's price, and it does not recover. The floor is permanent.</p>
      <div class="itable-wrap">
        <table class="itable">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Item</th><th class="num-col">Price floor</th><th class="num-col">Units to reach it</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><span class="mc-icos"><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/emerald.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /></span>Emerald</td><td class="num-col">65%</td><td class="num-col">1,077</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="mc-icos"><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/raw_copper.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/copper_ingot.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/charcoal.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /></span>Copper, charcoal</td><td class="num-col">75%</td><td class="num-col">1,438</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="mc-icos"><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/raw_iron.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/iron_ingot.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/raw_gold.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/gold_ingot.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /></span>Iron, gold</td><td class="num-col">85%</td><td class="num-col">2,031</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="mc-icos"><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/coal.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/redstone.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/lapis_lazuli.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /><img class="mc-ico" src="/assets/mc/quartz.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /></span>Coal, redstone, lapis, quartz</td><td class="num-col">85%</td><td class="num-col">3,250</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="money">
      <h2>Money</h2>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-money"></div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Money supply</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">Total currency held by players.</div>
        <div data-slot="supply-chart"></div>
      </div>
      <h3>At the counters</h3>
      <p class="as-sub">The Buy and Sell counters are the only places currency is created or destroyed outright, so a persistently positive net is the early warning that something is mispriced.</p>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="mint"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="prices">
      <h2>Prices</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">Medians of active chest-shop prices, not fixed rates, with the 7-day change and 30-day trend.</p>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-prices"></div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Price index</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">A fixed basket of wheat, iron, diamonds, ender pearls and oak logs. Base 100 at launch.</div>
        <div data-slot="price-chart"></div>
      </div>
      <div data-slot="item-table"></div>
      <h3>Daily range</h3>
      <p class="as-sub">Open, high, low and close per item, from chest-shop sales.</p>
      <div class="candles" data-slot="candles"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="trade">
      <h2>Trade</h2>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-trade"></div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Trade volume</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">Value moving between players and through shops each day.</div>
        <div data-slot="volume-chart"></div>
      </div>
      <h3>Volume leaders, last 24h</h3>
      <div data-slot="volume-table"></div>
      <h3>The index</h3>
      <p class="as-sub">A weekly verdict computed from that volume. It needs eight active traders and fourteen days of history before it will judge.</p>
      <div class="mei" data-slot="mei" data-code="INSUFFICIENT_DATA">
        <div class="mei-top"><span class="mei-label">Loading&hellip;</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="wealth">
      <h2>Wealth</h2>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-wealth"></div>
      <div data-slot="wealth-table"></div>
    </section>

    <details class="method">
      <summary>How the Meridian Economic Index is calculated</summary>
      <div class="m-body">
        <p>The index reads the server's economy log (every balance change), the land databases, and the shop transaction history. It needs at least <strong>8 active traders</strong> and <strong>14 days</strong> of history before it will assign a state. Each week it compares the last 7 days of trade volume against the 7 days before that:</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Expansion</dt><dd>Trade volume up more than 10% week over week.</dd>
          <dt>Steady</dt><dd>Trade volume within a &minus;5% to +10% band. A healthy, consistent market.</dd>
          <dt>Cooling</dt><dd>Trade volume down 5% to 25%. Activity is slowing.</dd>
          <dt>Recession</dt><dd>Trade volume down more than 25%, week over week.</dd>
          <dt>Insufficient data</dt><dd>Not enough players or history to judge.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>The <strong>Gini</strong> figure measures how concentrated wealth is: <code>0</code> means everyone holds the same, <code>1</code> means one player holds everything. The <strong>price index</strong> tracks a fixed basket of wheat, iron, diamonds, ender pearls and oak logs against the median player-shop price for each, set to 100 at launch. Everything on this page refreshes automatically through the day.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</main>
</Base>
